From 937eb1ed5784019f82c3cae44d744252e0e3afad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:08:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homalawn label gap: the visible gap from the icon's shape to
 the label

homar_label_gap_dp now means one thing: the visible distance, in dp,
from the bottom of the icon's visible shape to the top of the label's
capitals. 0 (also unset) = the capitals touch the shape, never overlap.

Before, on the fixed grid the setting added dp to upstream's padding
and then clamped the result to the room left in the cell, so gap 0 was
upstream's -14 px on a 4x8 grid (label inside the icon's picture),
every positive gap hit the clamp (2 dp == 4 dp) and nothing between was
reachable. The added dp also fed upstream's fit-to-height pass, which
shrinks the grid and applies the label size factor a second time, so
the label's size could change with the gap.

The label padding is now round(gap * density) - shape margin - cap
inset: the shape margin is the transparent band below the visible shape
(upstream's 0.92 visible-area model), the cap inset how far the label's
capitals start below the top of its text line, measured with the
label's own font (Lawnchair's workspace font as FontManager applies it)
at its own size. It is fitted on the fixed grid once the cell's final
height is known (after the workspace and cell layout paddings), after
upstream sized and fitted everything with its own padding, so the gap
moves the label and nothing else. The gap is held at the most the cell
has room for (the icon at the cell's top, the label line ending at its
bottom); the block the cell centres uses the same padding and line,
never taller than the cell, so every gap from 0 up to that maximum
lands exactly. Responsive and scalable grids keep upstream's padding. A
workspace font change, or a provider font arriving, reloads the grid so
the metrics follow it.

launcher.device_profile reports icon.label_gap {dp, max_dp,
shape_margin, cap_inset, line_height, icon_block} so the desktop offers
only reachable gaps and draws any gap as the phone would; the debug
build's debug_home_views reads the label's padding, line and cap inset
back from the view.
